course: dictionary
lesson: 9500
title: Family words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stepparent is the person who is married to your mother or father but is not your birth parent. The word is made of step and parent, and it tells you the family is made by marriage, not by birth. Read the words around it to check.
explain: «New stepparents take time; feeling angry at first is normal, and doing small things together can help people get on.» Take time and small things together are the clues. They show that getting on as a new family is slow and gradual, and that feelings can be mixed at the start.
explain: Sometimes the sentence explains the word for you. «"Blended family" means a family with a stepparent and stepchildren.» Here the author gives you the meaning straight away. When that happens, swap the meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A stepparent is married to your mother or father, but is not your birth parent.
fact: A stepmother is a stepparent who is a woman. A stepfather is a stepparent who is a man.
fact: «Blended family» means a family with a stepparent and stepchildren.
fact: Fairy tales often show a wicked stepmother, but most real stepparents are caring.
fact: Related words include stepbrother, stepsister and stepchild.
exercise: What is a stepparent? | A parent who is your birth mother or father | *The person married to your mother or father who is not your birth parent | A brother or sister you were born with | A grandparent who lives nearby
exercise: «Blended family» means what? | *A family with a stepparent and stepchildren | A family that goes on holiday together every year | A family that always lives in one house | A family that has only one child
exercise: «New stepparents take time; feeling angry at first is normal.» What does this sentence suggest? | Stepparents are always angry with their children | *Getting on as a new family can take time, and mixed feelings at first are normal | Angry feelings should be hidden straight away | Stepfamilies never work well
test: Which word means a stepparent who is a man? | stepsister | stepchild | stepmother | *stepfather
test: Fill in the gap: most real stepparents are ___. | wicked | lazy | *caring | cruel
exam: Which sentence uses stepparent correctly? | My stepfather is the name of the school I go to. | *My stepmother helped me with my homework, and she is married to my dad. | My stepparent is my twin sister who was born on the same day as me. | A stepparent is a type of fish that lives in rivers.
